{{!-- A page's own media line, near the top of the page body and never in the
      hero. The hashtag uses the shared hashtag token: a live link to its
      gallery when media carries it, a resting token otherwise, so a visitor
      always reads the tag that finds this page's media. When media exists the
      gallery link sits beside it and opens the same gallery, so media presence
      shows as two agreeing signals in one place.
      Hash arguments: id (the line's anchor, set only when media exists, so a
      jump link never lands on a line with nothing to open), display (the
      hashtag), galleryHref (null without media), galleryLabel (the gallery
      link's label). --}}
<p class="media-line"{{#if galleryHref}} id="{{id}}"{{/if}}>
  {{#if galleryHref}}
  <a class="hashtag hashtag--media" href="{{galleryHref}}">{{display}}</a>
  <a class="action-link" href="{{galleryHref}}">{{galleryLabel}}</a>
  {{else}}
  <span class="hashtag">{{display}}</span>
  {{/if}}
</p>
